    "raw": "{\"ruleId\":\"item-77d3bb2dedc0\",\"class\":\"not\",\"constraints\":[],\"coverage\":\"\",\"residual\":\"Does the agent's final message hand the human a task it could have done itself (for example asking them to run or type a command, contact someone, or ask X) that is not human-only (biometric auth, payment, physical action) and for which this turn's tool calls show no record of the agent trying and failing?\",\"probes\":null,\"rationale\":\"Each delegating phrase is allowed when the task is human-only or when the transcript records a failed attempt. A line pattern on the final message cannot tell whether the task needs a human. It also cannot check that no failed attempt appears elsewhere in the transcript. So any literal match would wrongly fail permitted handoffs. Deciding requires judging what the delegated task means and whether the tool calls amount to a real attempt.\"}",
